## Full Meeting Flow (Step by Step)

```
1. POST /agents/login              → get access_token

2. POST /meetings/start            → get meeting_id

3. GET  /meetings/{id}/upload-url  → get presigned S3 URL + s3_key

4. PUT  <presigned_url>            → upload audio bytes directly to S3

5. POST /meetings/{id}/chunk       → API fetches from S3, sends to Whisper
   (body: s3_key=...)                + Diarization in parallel, appends
                                      diarized text to meeting.transcript
                                      (repeat steps 3-5 for each chunk)

6. POST /meetings/{id}/end         → status → "processing"
                                      meeting_id published to SQS

7. [osf-worker picks up SQS job]
   a. Reads meeting.transcript from Postgres
   b. Reads agent_context:{agent_id} from Redis
      (falls back to Postgres if cache miss)
   c. Builds prompt with company context injected
   d. POST http://ollama:11434/api/generate (phi3:mini, stream=False)
   e. Parses NDJSON response, extracts first line
   f. json.loads the model's response field
   g. Saves insights to meeting.insights, status → "done"
   h. Caches insights + coaching separately in Redis

8. GET /meetings/{id}/results      → poll until status = "done"
   (poll every 15s, up to 40 attempts = 10 minutes max)
```

