## Company Context Injection

When an agent uploads company context (pricing, policies, product info),
it is stored in Postgres and cached in Redis under `agent_context:{agent_id}`.

At analysis time, the worker injects it into the LLM prompt as:

```
COMPANY CONTEXT (use this to evaluate the agent's knowledge, pricing accuracy,
and alignment with company policy — flag any deviations in your coaching feedback):
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
<extracted_text>
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
```

This allows the AI to:
- Flag if an agent quoted the wrong price
- Identify if payment terms were misrepresented
- Catch unauthorised discounts being offered
- Coach against company policy violations specifically

Agents without context uploaded receive the same prompt minus this block —
fully backward compatible.

